## PR Title
Support complex std::randomize patterns using args replacement strategy (#6736)

## PR Description
Implements an argument-replacement strategy for `std::randomize()` that supports:

1. Array-element arguments (e.g. `std::randomize(arr[i])` inside `foreach` loops)
2. Mixed argument types (`VarRef`, `MemberSel`, `ArraySel` in the same call)

Mechanically:
- All arguments are replaced with `__Varg*` reference parameters
- A `similarNode` matching predicate is added so semantic equality works across the three node types
- `__Varg*` are excluded from being re-captured by `CaptureVisitor`
- Null-pointer guards are added for robustness

Closes issue #6736 ("Support ArraySel in foreach case and Mixed arguments types case in std::randomize"). 31 commits in total. Coverage at merge: 100% line, 75% branch.

